// 0.0.10 T01 std library: `result` module — the `Result` declaration.
//
//     pub enum Result<T, E> {
//         Ok(T),
//         Err(E),
//     }
//
// This declaration is the **language-level source of truth** (0.0.10 PLAN
// D1): it parses through the ordinary 0.0.7 parameterized-enum frontend,
// and the compiler recognizes `std.result.Result` by canonical path and
// maps it onto its internal builtin representation. The runtime keeps the
// 0.0.2 encoding unchanged (`PackOk` / `PackErr` / `IsErr` / `UnwrapOk` /
// `UnwrapErr`, 0xA0–0xA4; `FieldTypeTag::Result = 6`; the VM's
// `Value::Ok` / `Value::Err`) — no `enum_defs` entry is emitted for this
// declaration and no variant codegen runs: the module is declaration-only.
//
// `import std.result;` imports the `Result` name; its `Ok` / `Err`
// variants travel with the export. The declaration cannot be shadowed or
// re-declared: an `enum Result` anywhere outside this module is rejected
// (D1 "What this locks"). Prelude registration of the trio is 0.0.10 D2 /
// T02 territory and is documented there when it lands.
//
// The module holds no functions. `?` propagation and choose-on-Result keep
// their exact 0.0.2/0.0.9 semantics and lowering (0.0.10 D3).
pub enum Result<T, E> {
    Ok(T),
    Err(E),
}
